{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-23597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1)={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\n$$\n\nThen, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1)={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-23597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nThen, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-65402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the following identities: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the parentheses and use the above identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{1}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }-1 \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta ({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-23796" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23796" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta +1"] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23796" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-1+{sin}^{2}⁡x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-1+{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-1+{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n1-{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-1+{sin}^{2}⁡x & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-(1-{sin}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡x}}{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡x}}-\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-2{cos}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}-1+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1-2{cos}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-120652" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120652" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "1-2{cos}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "{cos}^{2}⁡x+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120652" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-2{cos}^{2}⁡x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}=\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-120655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +1"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify ${sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we can simplify our expression by factoring it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x & =({sec}^{2}⁡x)^{2}-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+({tan}^{2}⁡x)^{2} \\\\  & ={({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}^{2} & ={(1)}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-23853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-23853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression by factoring it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)^{2}} & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-120661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}"] ["math" "\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-43292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-43292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the following identities: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nUsing the above identity, we can simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1) & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={tan}^{4}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ={tan}^{4}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-43292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-43292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-43292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-43292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression by factoring the numerator as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1 & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}}-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/ma