n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the numerator as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-65392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)"] ["math" "-(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)"] ["math" "-1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-74167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-74167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1 & ={tan}^{2}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)-1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡x({tan}^{2}⁡x)-1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{4}⁡x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{4}⁡x-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-74167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-74167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-74167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+{tan}^{4}⁡x"] ["math" "1-{tan}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x"] ["math" "{tan}^{4}⁡x-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-74167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{tan}^{4}⁡x-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x+1}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x+1} & =\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can use $(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x+1} & =\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x})}^{2} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x+1}={cos}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-120807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{cos}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1"] ["math" "{cos}^{2}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{cos}^{2}⁡x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1} & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡x}}{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}⁡x}({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x})}^{2} \\\\  & ={cot}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{4}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1}={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-120667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x"] ["math" "{cot}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "{cot}^{2}⁡x-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{cot}^{2}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +1}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +1}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression and use again $(2)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }({tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)}{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & =({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)-1 \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +1}{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-120666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +2"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-120666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1+{tan}^{2}⁡x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1+{sec}^{2}⁡x-1\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression and use again $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1+{sec}^{2}⁡x-1 & ={sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+\\cancel{1}+{sec}^{2}⁡x-\\cancel{1} \\\\  & ={sec}^{4}⁡x-{sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡x-1) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x+1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "397df3e28324dc03f1af81ebd0e414b303735a85e3cccadab8441eb59c5def31"} {"question" "q-65401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡x{tan}^{4}⁡x"] ["math" "{sec}^{4}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "q-65401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{sec}^{2}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0b39a65f1d3e183571e568d503c69b1c6896bca82d06e964fb26ed0ca50873"} {"question" "e-3455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/example-3455.json" "file_sha256" "92253fc495dbfa2df00a6776b0ec9f5a99ba723b72082d3354cf86e2685ec278"} {"question" "e-3455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta} =  \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue} 1} = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta} = 1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/example-3455.json" "file_sha256" "92253fc495dbfa2df00a6776b0ec9f5a99ba723b72082d3354cf86e2685ec278"} {"question" "e-3463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/example-3463.json" "file_sha256" "f85fe5f58f5813da9ea79115125466634f8bf3c523da4bb2185e1368c000452d"} {"question" "e-3463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\sec{\\theta}+\\tan{\\theta}} = \\dfrac{\\color{blue}\\sec^2{\\theta} - \\tan^2{\\theta}}{\\sec{\\theta} + \\tan{\\theta}}\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression by factoring the numerator as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )}}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta} =  \\sec{\\theta} - \\tan{\\theta}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/example-3463.json" "file_sha256" "f85fe5f58f5813da9ea79115125466634f8bf3c523da4bb2185e1368c000452d"} {"question" "e-3144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\tan^2 x\\sec^2 x - \\tan^4 x +1$ in terms of $\\sec x$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/example-3144.json" "file_sha256" "9bb4279c2ef2ff459e23974440cd3494c9458baf1076304ecbd138998f16883c"} {"question" "e-3144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{4}⁡x+1 & ={tan}^{2}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)+1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡x\\cdot (1)+1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can use $(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡x+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x\\sec^2 x - \\tan^4 x +1 = \\sec^2 x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997351/example-3144.json" "file_sha256" "9bb4279c2ef2ff459e23974440cd3494c9458baf1076304ecbd138998f16883c"}] "usage" {"q-65392" [] "e-3455" [] "e-3144" [] "e-3463" []} "basis" 1072 "retractions" [[17592186188889 :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{1}{\\sec x - \\tan x}$."] [17592186188124 :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta}$."] [17592186188124 :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(1) & 1 + \\tan^{2} θ = \\sec^{2} θ \\\\ (2) & \\tan^{2} θ = \\sec^{2} θ - 1 \\\\ (3) & \\sec^{2} θ - \\tan^{2} θ = 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta} = \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue} 1} = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta} = 1\n$$"] [17592186188125 :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta}$."] [17592186188125 :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(1) & 1 + \\tan^{2} θ = \\sec^{2} θ \\\\ (2) & \\tan^{2} θ = \\sec^{2} θ - 1 \\\\ (3) & \\sec^{2} θ - \\tan^{2} θ = 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\sec{\\theta}+\\tan{\\theta}} = \\dfrac{\\color{blue}\\sec^2{\\theta} - \\tan^2{\\theta}}{\\sec{\\theta} + \\tan{\\theta}}\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression by factoring the numerator as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sec^{2} θ - \\tan^{2} θ}{\\sec θ + \\tan θ} &= ((\\sec θ - \\tan θ)(\\sec θ + \\tan θ))/(\\sec θ + \\tan θ) \\\\\n&= ((\\sec θ - \\tan θ)(\\sec θ + \\tan θ))/((\\sec θ + \\tan θ)) \\\\\n&= \\sec θ - \\tan θ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta} = \\sec{\\theta} - \\tan{\\theta}\n$$"] [17592186188123 :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(1) & 1 + \\tan^{2} x = \\sec^{2} x \\\\ (2) & \\tan^{2} x = \\sec^{2} x - 1 \\\\ (3) & \\sec^{2} x - \\tan^{2} x = 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan^{2} x\\sec^{2} x - \\tan^{4} x + 1 &= \\tan^{2} x(\\sec^{2} x - \\tan^{2} x) + 1 \\\\\n&= \\tan^{2} x \\cdot (1) + 1 \\\\\n&= \\tan^{2} x + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can use $(1)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan^{2} x + 1 &= \\sec^{2} x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x\\sec^2 x - \\tan^4 x +1 = \\sec^2 x\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186187815 17592186187816 17592186187817 17592186187818 17592186187819] "immutable_fields" [[17592186187814 :answer-field/correct] [17592186187814 :answer-field/id] [17592186187814 :answer-field/key] [17592186187814 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
